    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298-a1">

                <pb facs="0753" n="716" xml:id="pg716"/>


                <p>In your discretion, if it seems appropriate, you may indicate to Zahedi that it
                    might be advisable for him to continue negotiations with Soviets or at least not
                    make first move to break them off. Such an attitude would be in line nationalist
                    policies expected of Zahedi and would, if Soviets refuse pay gold or make
                    concessions, be another black mark against Russians in Iran. However, Zahedi
                    should not obtain impression American public would be unconcerned if his Govt
                    made any considerable concessions to Soviets.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
